      <ul>
        <li>When cutting calories, your protein target goes up to 1.6g/kg — not down</li>
        <li>Without enough protein in a deficit, your body loses muscle alongside fat</li>
        <li>Lifting 2–3 times a week is the other half — protein is the raw material, training is the signal to keep muscle</li>
        <li>High protein during weight loss helps preserve muscle, burns more calories in digestion, and reduces hunger</li>
        <li>The scale can go down while you're actually getting worse — unless protein is high enough</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

