    </div>

    <div class="prose">

      <p>
        The conventional weight loss advice for men over 40 goes something like this: eat less, move more, cut the junk. That advice isn't wrong. But it's dangerously incomplete — because it ignores the one variable that determines whether you lose fat or muscle when you're in a deficit.
      </p>

      <p>
        That variable is protein. And the counterintuitive truth is that when you're trying to lose weight, your protein target goes <em>up</em> — not down.
      </p>

      <!-- STAT BOXES -->
