      <p>
        The gap is real. A 180-pound man trying to lose weight needs about 131g of protein per day. The average man eats about 90g, and a man who's cutting portions across the board usually eats less than that. A 40g-a-day shortfall, every day of a diet, is exactly how muscle gets lost.
      </p>

      <div class="link-box">
